OL,3,CProgramme listings for MON 25 MAY
OL,4,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,5,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,6,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,7,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,8,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,9,     Geverything in between.
OL,10,G2330F'Round Midnight
OL,11,     GBritish trumpeter Byron Wallen
OL,12,     Gselects three of his best-loved
OL,13,     Grecords by Miles Davis to
OL,14,     Gcelebrate the centenary of one of
OL,15,     Gthe most influential figures in
OL,16,     G20th-century music.
OL,17,G0030FThrough the Night
OL,18,     GEva Ollikainen conducts the WDR
OL,19,     GSymphony Orchestra, Cologne in
OL,20,     GStrauss' tone poem 'A Hero's
OL,21,     GLife'. Penny Gore presents.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
